// ============================================================================
// POST-ENHANCEMENT ANALYSIS RESULT
// ============================================================================
// WHAT: The EXACT SAME endpoint and response shape as 01-analyze.jsonc.
// The only difference is what you SEND it: postEnhancement=true plus the
// enhanced query text, so the AI re-scores the freshly-enhanced query
// instead of whatever is currently saved on the rule.
//
// IMPORTANT: analysis.analysisType in the DB/response is still the literal
// string "analyze" — NOT "post_enhance". The "Post-Enhancement" label you
// see in the UI history table is applied client-side based on context
// (that this analysis followed an enhance operation), not a distinct
// backend record type.
//
// WHEN: User clicks "Analyze After Enhancement" right after an Enhance result
// is shown, to independently verify the AI's own rewrite actually improved
// the rule before committing to it.
//
// ENDPOINT: POST /api/analysis/analyze   (status 201, same route as Analyze)
// SOURCE:   src/app/api/analysis/analyze/route.ts
//
// REQUEST BODY (note: query is the ENHANCED text, sent explicitly — not
// re-read from the DB, so it scores exactly what would be applied):
//   {
//     "ruleId": "uuid",
//     "query": "<the enhanced query text>",
//     "postEnhancement": true
//   }
// ============================================================================

